    "turn_text": "Others disagreed with me, including others I work with. But I just had the sense that this campaign where you had two candidates seeking redemption from 2010 losses, both filling the pressure and the desire to sort of retool themselves and not only sort of make amends for that, if you will, if that's how you want to look at, but also define their vision for the Commonwealth moving forward, and needing to do that in the context of, frankly, the Deval Patrick administration, where he remains still a very popular political figure, You know, Charlie couldn't do as he did in 2010, try to run a sort of a more angry campaign about had enough of Devolve Patrick. That was clearly not the case. And where Martha Cokley needed to try to run a campaign where she was close enough to this administration or policies, but at the same time create distance and share her own vision. And that's a very, those are difficult needles to thread for both candidates.",
