    "turn_idx": 88,
    "turn_text": "I really don't think so. But look, let me acknowledge to your listeners, you know, obviously, I have a particular bias here, but I think this has been a very successful administration. Look, you can list the challenges they've had to face over the last year in particular, but they're in any administration. Certainly, over eight years, there have been challenges. I think the hallmark of this administration is governor. is that when problems arise and they always arise in any administration. They take various shapes and sizes. The question is do you face them? I mean first of all you have to find them, face them and then fix them and I think that has been the hallmark of the Duval Patrick administration, the Duval Patrick's leadership, and it is a form of leadership, right? And, you know, I hope, like, all right-thinking people should hope that the Baker administration has absolutely no challenges or calamities on their watch. But I doubt that's going to be the case, and when they happen, I hope that the next administration does what this administration does. which is fix and find, face, and fix the problems, because they're going to come up. And Charlie Baker, above all else knows from his previous time here that those problems do come up. Now, Charlie Baker ran as a devolved Patrick Republican, right? He learned in 2010 what it actually takes to run a winning campaign here. And you look at some of his policy positions today. They're very different from where they were in 2010 and much closer to where Deval Patrick has been a long time.",
