    "turn_text": "don't necessarily think that means he needs to run for office again. And I don't think, you know, he wants to spend the next four years on TV or radio shows, second-guessing the next administration. That's not who he is. But I think he started this process. He ran for governor because he felt he had something to offer the people of Massachusetts. I think he's offered a great deal. And I encourage him to continue to have that voice. You know, everything he says to me, which is what he says to everyone else publicly, is, you know, we are watching the waning days of his elected life. And I take him at his word. And I don't see him taking a post in the current Obama administration. He's committed to returning to private life. And to me, that doesn't mean he can't continue to have a public voice.",
