    "turn_idx": 105,
    "turn_text": "doesn't know it yet, right? But I'm going to start a super PAC. No, seriously. When the governor appointed me, I said exactly what I meant at the time, which was, I had no intentions of running for office, not that office or not any other. Although I will tell you this, and I'll just be in candid. You know, the more my experience in public service, both at the Statehouse here in Boston and in Washington, D.C., certainly gave me a deeper appreciation for the ability of those who hold those offices should they choose to have really, really powerful and positive impact on people. And I'll be honest with you, that's a luring. It's attractive to be empowered to help other people. I don't know what the future holds. Well, look, check with me in 10 years. I'll let you know what I'm thinking in. For the moment, like the governor, I'm enjoying private life, and I'm enjoying the time I have with my family. And except for the time I spent on the scrum, I'm enjoying being out of the public eye.",
